### Page 1 of 3

```text
Planning and Development Office
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282
(Fax) 307-637-6366

MEMORANDUM

TO:

Mayor Kaysen and City Council
FROM:
Development Department (Mike Tylka)
SUBJECT:
Holmes Corner Preliminary Plat - Updated Map Submission & Conditions
Clarification (UDC-15-00816)
DATE:
February 11, 2016
___________________________________________________________________________________________________________
Mayor Kaysen and City Council Members,

On Tuesday, February 2nd, the day after the Planning Commission Meeting, the agent for the Holmes
Corner Preliminary Plat submitted a document that sought to address Planning Commission conditions
and Staff concerns. On Thursday, February 4th, the agent and other members of the team sat down with
City Staff for the first time to discuss the project. In this meeting, all parties went over staff concerns,
Planning Commission Conditions, and how to move forward. The agent has addressed a number of Staff
concerns.

At this time Staff seeks to clarify earlier conditions and offer revised ones. Planning Commission
recommended the following:
1.) A determination be made in regards to current and future proposed zoning districts that may or
may not be sought at the site
2.) Right-of-way dedications be amended to reflect the Engineering Departments recommendations
3.) That BOPU, access, and drainage easements be addressed per the BOPU’s and City Staffs’
comments.

Staff would like to recommend edited Conditions One and Three and the elimination of Condition Two.
These read as follows:
1.) That Lots 3-5 be identified for future zoning of NR-3 Neighborhood Residential – High
Density or CB Community Business.
2.) That the Board of Public Utilities concerns are met in regards to the reuse water line
running through the property.

In addition, at the meeting on the 4th the agent stated that they would address Staff concerns regarding
street network connectivity and block size standards, as of the date of this memo the agent has not, and
therefore Staff is recommending a third condition as follows:
3.) That the applicant addresses street network connectivity and block size standards as
identified in the Unified Development Code.

Attached are the third set of maps submitted by the agent, dated February 3rd, 2016 that did not make it
into the City Council submission. Please do not hesitate to contact the Development Department to
discuss this matter further. Thank you.

A COMMUNITY OF CHOICE
 Development Department
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282 (Fax) 307-637-6366
```

